{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Answered the two gaps opened by the VerifyLeader premise correction and recorded its consequence in the account. The corrected entry now states that verifyLeader starts the vote count at one for the leader itself before sizing the voter-only quorum and registering the future on every replication stream, which makes the arithmetic explicit: in a three-voter configuration the quorum is two, the leader supplies one vote and a single non-voter acknowledgement completes the verification, while the control with the non-voters also cut has no second acknowledgement and fails. The rationale records that no conclusion, counterevidence item or limitation depended on the leader being excluded from the count, so no receipt needs reinterpretation. The first gap is answered by reviewing the current interpretation and the lease experiment against that mechanism, which they continue to support; the second is answered by noting that the preceding interpretation rests on the same receipts, asserted nothing about who supplies the votes beyond the non-voter stream completing the count, and remains valid as history. Both answers are marked resolved, the interpretation carries the full counterevidence and limitation lists so nothing is dropped, and the submission validates against submission.schema.json.\"}"}}
